<page xmlns="http://projectmallard.org/1.0/"
      type="guide" style="task" id="settings" xml:lang="C">

  <info>
    <link type="guide" xref="index#settings"/>
    <title type="link" role="trail">Babble Help</title>
    <title type="text">Settings</title>
    <title type="link">Settings</title>
    <desc>Interface text size, refresh, notifications, and the defaults a
    new post starts from.</desc>
  </info>

  <title>Settings</title>

  <section id="opening">
    <title>Opening Preferences</title>
    <p>
      <link xref="keys">Ctrl+,</link> opens Preferences and it can be
      searched by typing.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="interface">
    <title>Interface</title>
    <p>
      It covers the interface text size and line height, how posts refresh,
      desktop and server notifications, and the defaults a new post
      starts from.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="server">
    <title>Server settings</title>
    <p>
      A few settings only reach as far as your server: default visibility,
      language and content warnings are stored in your server preferences,
      so they follow you to any other Mastodon client.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="language">
    <title>Language</title>
    <p>
      Changing the interface language takes effect the next time Babble
      starts.
    </p>
  </section>

</page>